# Closed-pose interference proof: the base latch must clear the folded lid's
# shell. `fitcheck` renders that intersection and must be EMPTY — the strip
# stands `latch_clear` outboard of the wall face, and the folded lid's own front
# wall lands on the band the strip used to occupy. `fitcheck_neg` rebuilds the
# strip flush inside that band (clear = -wall_t), which is the geometry this
# design shipped with, and MUST render non-empty: 216.00 mm³ across 32 facets
# (issue #230).
#
# This is the guard that catches a closed-pose clash. Nothing else here can:
# the design prints FLAT, so every existing check — the default render, the
# preview sheet, printcheck, the test slice — looks at a pose where the two
# halves are 76 mm apart, scores it watertight and clean, and never folds it.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
